    <Placemark>
      <name>⚠ Elk River</name>
      <styleUrl>#pt_restricted</styleUrl>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Elk River</b><br/>Curry, Southwest<br/>Power boats allowed &mdash; seaplane-capable.<br/>Motor use: Default: motors allowed unless a rule below applies<br/><br/><b>&#9888; Oregon boating rules on this waterway</b><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Elk River: No motors over 25 horsepower<br/>A person must not use an internal combustion motor rated over 25 horsepower to propel a boat downstream of the Ironhead ramp.<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0082">Oregon OAR rule</a><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Elk River: electric motors only<br/>A person must not use an internal combustion motor of any size to propel a boat upstream of the Ironhead ramp<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0082">Oregon OAR rule</a><br/><br/><a href="https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/1510/main">Waterway details</a>]]></description>
      <Point>
