    <Placemark>
      <name>⚠ Grande Ronde River</name>
      <styleUrl>#pt_restricted</styleUrl>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Grande Ronde River</b><br/>Wallowa, Northeast<br/>Power boats allowed &mdash; seaplane-capable.<br/>Motor use: Default: motors allowed unless a rule below applies<br/><br/><b>&#9888; Oregon boating rules on this waterway</b><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Grande Ronde River: no motors - downstream of Umatilla NF boundary<br/>No motor use between the Umatilla National Forest Boundary (1.5 miles below the confluence with the Wallowa River at approximately RM 80) downstream to the Oregon/Washington state line; except for landowner access for land management activities<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0340">Oregon OAR rule</a>]]></description>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-117.85244,45.60047,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
