    <Placemark>
      <name>⚠ Rogue River (Upper)</name>
      <styleUrl>#pt_restricted</styleUrl>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Rogue River (Upper)</b><br/>Jackson, Southwest<br/>Power boats allowed &mdash; seaplane-capable.<br/>Motor use: Default: motors allowed unless a rule below applies<br/><br/><b>&#9888; Oregon boating rules on this waterway</b><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Rogue River: Motors restricted when three-day average flow is measured by USGS to be below 1350 CFS at Dodge Bridge.<br/>Motors restricted from Fishers Ferry to Dodge Bridge when the three-day average flow decreases below 1350 CFS, as read from the USGS River Gauge at Dodge Bridge.<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0151">Oregon OAR rule</a><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Rogue River: No motor use greater than 15 HP above Dodge Bridge, and all Tributaries of the Rogue River from Fishers Ferry to Lost Creek Dam.<br/>No motor use greater than 15 HP on the main stem of the Rogue River above Dodge Bridge County Park and ALL Rogue River tributaries, between Fishers Ferry County Park and William L. Jess Dam, (Lost Creek Dam).<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0151">Oregon OAR rule</a><br/><b>Motor Restriction</b>: Rogue River: No motor use greater than 15 HP on all Rogue River Tributaries above Fishers Ferry.<br/>No motor use greater than 15 HP on all Rogue River Tributaries above Fishers Ferry.<br/><a href="https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/view.action?ruleNumber=250-020-0151">Oregon OAR rule</a>]]></description>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-122.84736,42.53566,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
